# secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# data — ignored by default, with a deliberate carve-out below.
#
#   data/raw/      NOT committed. Contains Datastream/LSEG-derived series
#                  (basis_waha.csv, basis_domsouth.csv). That data is licensed
#                  to the university, not to us — republishing it would breach
#                  the licence. Everything here is regenerable from the fetch
#                  functions in src/storage_stress/data/connectivity.py.
#   data/live/     NOT committed. Live paper ledgers (books.db, xsec_books.db)
#                  and run logs. Binary, and they mutate every trading day, so
#                  committing them would produce a noisy diff on every mark.
#   data/processed/ COMMITTED (see carve-out). These are the research outputs
#                  the results write-up cites as evidence — the agent ladder,
#                  null distributions and equity curves. ~730 KB, static once
#                  written. A reader must be able to check the numbers.
# NOTE ON THE PATTERN BELOW: it must be `data/*`, not `data/`. Git does not
# descend into a directory excluded by a trailing-slash pattern, so a later
# negation inside it can never match — `data/` + `!data/processed/` silently
# ignores everything. Excluding the CONTENTS (`data/*`) keeps the directory
# walkable so the re-includes below actually fire.
data/*
!data/processed/
data/processed/*
!data/processed/*.csv
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/

# generated documents
#
# The PDF and DOCX deliverables are BUILD OUTPUTS, not source. Their source is
# the matching .md in docs/, which is committed. Regenerate with:
#     python scripts/md_to_pdf.py
# Keeping binaries out means the .md stays the single source of truth — no
# risk of a committed PDF drifting out of sync with the text it came from,
# and no unreviewable binary diffs in the history.
docs/pdf/
docs/docx/

# notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/
notebooks/scratch/

# os / editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
